From 4d523f8a8bc5c0100982955216f539dc085b13ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arealjim <6187715+arealjim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:00:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/23] runtime: encoder_full_range skips the per-frame
 video-range conversion

Config encoder_full_range (default false): the low-latency rtvc or software
VideoToolbox session is fed the compose BGRA surface directly instead of a
BT.709 video-range 4:2:0 conversion of each frame, which costs about 1 ms of
submit per frame (measured 2026-10-17, M5 Pro, 2272x1264). Those sessions
then write a full-range stream and signal it in the VUI, so only clients that
honour the signalled range may use it (the Steam Frame client does since
2026-10-17). The .ave. hardware session writes video range from BGRA either
way and is unaffected.

